s was ... \",\"title\":\"https://societyofauthors.org/2024/06/20/spanning-genres-showing-outstanding-depths-celebrating-the-2024-society-of-authors-awards-winners/\"}],\"query\":\"author grew up city prize winner born same city\"},{\"cached\":false,\"hits\":[{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"previously_received\":false,\"ref\":\"d22\",\"snippet\":\" ... Daniel Halpern was born in Syracuse, New York, grew up in Los Angeles and Seattle, and has lived in Tangier, Morocco, New York City and Princeton. He is the author of nine collections of poetry, most recently Something Shining. For 25 years, Halpern edited the international literary magazine ... \",\"title\":\"https://centerforfiction.org/grants-awards/medal-for-editorial-excellence/medal-for-editorial-excellence-past-recipients/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"previously_received\":false,\"ref\":\"d4\",\"snippet\":\" ... Smith is the author of three acclaimed books of poetry: The Body's Question, winner of the Cave Canem Poetry Prize; Duende, winner of the James Laughlin Award of the Academy of American Poets and an Essence Literary Award; and, most recently, Life on Mars, winner of the ... \",\"title\":\"https://griffinpoetryprize.com/judges/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"previously_received\":false,\"ref\":\"d23\",\"snippet\":\" ... Giller Prize shortlisted - Alligator\\n\\n2003:Winterset Award for Excellence in Newfoundland Writing - Open\\n\\n2002: Giller Prize short-listed - Open\\n\\nCanadian Authors Association Jubilee Award (short fiction)\\n\\nMar 15 Camilla Gibb\\n\\nMar 29 Larissa Lai\\n\\nLarissa Lai was born in California in 1967. She grew up in Newfoundland, and ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.yorku.ca/laps/huma/canadian-writers/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"previously_received\":false,\"ref\":\"d17\",\"snippet\":\" ... literary journals, and is the award-winning author of three poetry collections and the novel Salt Houses. She lives in New York City.\\n\\nWha